==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Neo Psychocat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Corrupted Psychocat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Psychocat is a very useful support cat for nearly all of [[Into the Future]] and some parts of [[Cats of the Cosmos]]. Alongside [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Surfer Cat]], Psychocat is exceptional at controlling short-ranged Alien enemies and keeping their threat level to a minimum. Stacks of Psychocats keep Alien enemies at a distance while your [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien]] heavy hitters like [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg]] and [[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Chill Cat]] beat them to a pulp, he also outranges both [[Raging Bahamut Cat]] and [[Corrupted Valkyrie]], allowing you to paralyze them so your ranged attackers can safely take them out.

In the [[Legend Stages]], Psychocat is rarely effective, as his lack of area attack limits his use to stages with few Alien frontliners. He can still effectively slow [[Cosmic Cyclone]], [[Nimoy Bore]] and similar units to great effect, though.

==='''True Form'''===
Corrupted Psychocat gains more health, double speed and faster attacks. These improvements work together in massively increasing the number of attacks that a Psychocat can expect to land in his lifetime, leading to much more consistent slowing. His use does not change and his lack of area attack is not fixed, but the buff is easily worth the [[Catfruit]].

==='''Talents'''===
Target [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] expands Corrupted Psychocat's use to another trait, making him effective against, notably, [[Zyclone]] and [[Lord Gravey]]. Unlike the original anti-zombies [[Gardener Cat (Rare Cat)|Weedwacker Cat]] and [[Welterweight Cat (Rare Cat)|Ectoweight Cat]], however, he is powerless against unburrowing or reviving zombies, resulting is an overall bad matchup. Defense Buff doesn't drastically increase his survivability, but is helpful regardless. [[Weaken|Weaken]] and Slow Up improve his performance directly, but not by much, with weaken being just a -30% attack power that can override stronger weaken effects and slow being a 25% duration up at best.

Resist Freeze is extremely situational, as Corrupted Psychocat is unlikely to survive hits from most [[:Category:Enemies with Freeze ability|freezing enemies]] in the first place.

==='''Orb'''===
Defense Up against Aliens (or Zombies, if target Zombie is unlocked); any other Orb would be wasted. Note that even a Defense Up Orb against a trait he targets would rarely make a difference, so saving your high level Orbs for other cats is recommended.

Ability orbs are mostly the same story. Death Mini-Surge can provide a sort of Area Attack once in a blue moon, but there are far better units to use this orb on.

